            "text": "### 🏛️ Stage 2 Model Execution & Verification\n\nThe illustrative Stage 2 architectural additions for **AB-01 Courtyard Learning Centre** have been modeled, readback-verified, and mounted in the 3D Model viewer in solid display mode.\n\n---\n\n### 📋 Elements Summary & Verification\n\n```mindmap\nAB-01 Stage 2 Model\n  Levels\n    Ground Floor (0 mm)\n    Upper Floor (3600 mm)\n  Walls (16 total)\n    8 Ground Floor boundary walls\n    8 Upper Floor boundary walls\n  Openings (18 total)\n    Doors (6 total)\n      D-GF-01 (West courtyard wall)\n      D-GF-02 (North courtyard wall)\n      D-GF-03 (East courtyard wall)\n      D-UF-01 (West courtyard wall)\n      D-UF-02 (North courtyard wall)\n      D-UF-03 (East courtyard wall)\n    Windows (12 total)\n      W-GF-W1, W-GF-W2 (GF West)\n      W-GF-N1, W-GF-N2 (GF North)\n      W-GF-E1, W-GF-E2 (GF East)\n      W-UF-W1, W-UF-W2 (UF West)\n      W-UF-N1, W-UF-N2 (UF North)\n      W-UF-E1, W-UF-E2 (UF East)\n  Slabs (34 total)\n    Building Slabs (7 total)\n    Stair Treads (23 total)\n    Site Slab (1 total)\n    Courtyard Pond (1 total)\n    Planter Beds (2 total)\n  Roofs (3 total)\n```\n\n---\n\n### 🚪 Doors & Windows\n\n* **Courtyard Entry Doors (6 total, 1.2 m W × 2.4 m H)**:\n  * **Ground Floor**:\n    * `D-GF-01` (`10aa02db-d162-4967-bd6e-bb3e353542ca`): Hosted on `34326fca-431a-4d4f-be51-dd34f0920a26` (West wing, courtyard face), centered at offset 6,000 mm.\n    * `D-GF-02` (`4ca2d808-f6f1-4a58-badc-68381aa458b2`): Hosted on `201b0d64-fd2d-48c2-b675-f46879c6481c` (North wing, courtyard face), centered at offset 6,000 mm.\n    * `D-GF-03` (`6cea66a0-2a9c-4f53-95bf-0619e67c1208`): Hosted on `692a190a-c78c-4574-87cb-93fec89f700d` (East wing, courtyard face), centered at offset 6,000 mm.\n  * **Upper Floor** (*Conceptual openings for benchmark geometry only; no compliant access or constructability claimed*):\n    * `D-UF-01` (`fac82101-5dc6-4479-a048-ac3d4f2b1e24`): Hosted on `a426e762-5999-472e-a230-f8b7900bd4b1` (West wing, courtyard face), centered at offset 6,000 mm.\n    * `D-UF-02` (`edc6cc8c-6a92-467c-a38f-e7eb6a0c1d0a`): Hosted on `a920f31e-947c-478c-a2bf-d4880b929f3c` (North wing, courtyard face), centered at offset 6,000 mm.\n    * `D-UF-03` (`0ade4e46-7f87-4b78-83fa-ea1e7d644374`): Hosted on `33108938-bb25-4575-948f-a39b0fc937ed` (East wing, courtyard face), centered at offset 6,000 mm.\n\n* **Exterior Windows (12 total, 1.8 m W × 1.5 m H, 0.9 m sill)**:\n  * **Ground Floor Outer Perimeter**:\n    * West wall (`0c36c356-ef2d-4fc6-bfb9-d97b476bff2e`): `W-GF-W1` (offset 6,000 mm) & `W-GF-W2` (offset 12,000 mm).\n    * North wall (`95bfd96f-24bf-47c7-9b30-33aa1543507e`): `W-GF-N1` (offset 8,000 mm) & `W-GF-N2` (offset 16,000 mm).\n    * East wall (`89b5ba53-2853-4b27-8946-07f894a94d87`): `W-GF-E1` (offset 6,000 mm) & `W-GF-E2` (offset 12,000 mm).\n  * **Upper Floor Outer Perimeter**:\n    * West wall (`b0ecba24-8c98-406f-811c-127ac4ff33f9`): `W-UF-W1` (offset 6,000 mm) & `W-UF-W2` (offset 12,000 mm).\n    * North wall (`eb5a2608-e831-49df-b931-8af384d75e44`): `W-UF-N1` (offset 8,000 mm) & `W-UF-N2` (offset 16,000 mm).\n    * East wall (`c08cee0c-7f70-4d63-9b78-c59d8b23a3dc`): `W-UF-E1` (offset 6,000 mm) & `W-UF-E2` (offset 12,000 mm).\n  * All windows are positioned clear of doors and evenly spaced along their respective exterior wall spans.\n\n---\n\n### 🪜 Internal Stair Geometry\n\n* **Classification Disclosure**: The stair is a **geometric approximation** constructed using 23 discrete supported `slab` elements. The workbench schema does not possess a native parametric stair entity.\n* **Geometry & Spacing**:\n  * Positioned inside the reserved west-wing void ($X \\in [2400, 3600]\\,\\text{mm}$).\n  * 23 visible treads (`Tread-01` to `Tread-23`), each $1,200\\,\\text{mm}$ wide, $300\\,\\text{mm}$ deep, and $50\\,\\text{mm}$ thick, assigned material `\"Timber\"`.\n  * Rises: 24 equal rises of $150\\,\\text{mm}$ starting from ground level ($0\\,\\text{mm}$) up to the upper floor elevation ($3,600\\,\\text{mm}$).\n  * Alignment: Treads ascend from $Y = 5,700\\,\\text{mm}$ to $Y = 12,600\\,\\text{mm}$.\n  * Upper Floor Connection: The uppermost tread (`Tread-23`, offset $+3,450\\,\\text{mm}$, top edge at $Y = 12,600\\,\\text{mm}$) abuts the upper floor slab landing (`UF-Slab-West-North`, edge at $Y = 12,600\\,\\text{mm}$) with **$0\\,\\text{mm}$ horizontal gap**. The final $150\\,\\text{mm}$ rise steps directly onto the upper-floor finished slab level.\n  * The stairwell void remains open above the run, with no floor slabs obstructing the flight.\n\n---\n\n### 🌳 Site Slab & Courtyard Elements\n\n* **Site Slab** (`cb82ff24-6e88-49c6-990f-3d7e2e2ddb95`, `\"Site-Slab\"`):\n  * Dimensions: $32.0\\,\\text{m} \\times 26.0\\,\\text{m}$ ($X \\in [-4000, 28000]\\,\\text{mm}$, $Y \\in [-4000, 22000]\\,\\text{mm}$), providing uniform $4\\,\\text{m}$ margins around the $24\\,\\text{m} \\times 18\\,\\text{m}$ building envelope.\n  * Elevation & Thickness: Top at $-0.3\\,\\text{m}$ (offset $-300\\,\\text{mm}$), thickness $0.2\\,\\text{m}$ ($200\\,\\text{mm}$), material `\"Site Concrete\"`.\n\n* **Courtyard Pond** (`34e6e935-b7fd-4ae9-b995-b5ad13dfa8ab`, `\"Courtyard-Pond\"`):\n  * Dimensions: $6.0\\,\\text{m} \\times 3.0\\,\\text{m}$ ($X \\in [9000, 15000]\\,\\text{mm}$, $Y \\in [1000, 4000]\\,\\text{mm}$).\n  * Surface & Thickness: Top water surface at $-0.1\\,\\text{m}$ (offset $-100\\,\\text{mm}$), thickness $200\\,\\text{mm}$, material explicitly named `\"Water\"`.\n  * Placement: Centered horizontally in the southern courtyard zone, maintaining $\\ge 2,000\\,\\text{mm}$ clearance from all wing entry doors.\n\n* **Raised Planter Beds (2 total)**:\n  * West Bed (`60b8832f-2c69-4c44-a574-493aebfa6f96`, `\"Planter-Bed-West\"`): $4.0\\,\\text{m} \\times 1.0\\,\\text{m}$ ($X \\in [6500, 10500]\\,\\text{mm}$, $Y \\in [8500, 9500]\\,\\text{mm}$).\n  * East Bed (`f0486ac5-b329-458c-bc3c-aeb2b06885bb`, `\"Planter-Bed-East\"`): $4.0\\,\\text{m} \\times 1.0\\,\\text{m}$ ($X \\in [13500, 17500]\\,\\text{mm}$, $Y \\in [8500, 9500]\\,\\text{mm}$).\n  * Elevation & Thickness: Top at $+0.6\\,\\text{m}$ (offset $+600\\,\\text{mm}$), thickness $600\\,\\text{mm}$, material explicitly named `\"Planting\"`.\n  * Clearance: Separated by a central $3.0\\,\\text{m}$ walkway leading to the North courtyard door, clear of each other, pond, and all doorways.\n\n* **Renderer Material Display Disclosure**:\n  * While the materials are recorded as `\"Water\"` and `\"Planting\"` in the project data, the active solid 3D canvas uses a shared material shader with standard geometric shading. It does not provide physically distinct procedural water caustics, foliage textures, or transparency.\n\n---\n\n### 🔍 Verified Entity Counts & Limitations\n\n* **Design Status**: Revision `8`, saved and readback-verified.\n* **Storeys**: 2 levels (`Ground Floor` at $0\\,\\text{mm}$, `Upper Floor` at $3,600\\,\\text{mm}$).\n* **Walls**: 16 total exterior walls.\n* **Openings**: 18 total (6 doors, 12 windows).\n* **Slabs**: 34 total (1 GF building slab, 6 UF split slabs, 23 stair treads, 1 site slab, 1 pond slab, 2 planter bed slabs).\n* **Roofs**: 3 flat roof zones over the building footprint.\n* **Model Viewer**: Successfully mounted in solid display mode under scene hash `2dcfd3839480e59d885e603fb762d4bfd8b67e5874a3597d4616984704f79b76`.\n* **Remaining Limitations**: This benchmark model is an illustrative internal draft (`xray.internal-draft/1`). It is uncalibrated against real-world survey datum and does not represent an engineered, compliant, or construction-ready release. Upper-level courtyard doors function as conceptual geometric openings without balustrades or egress decks."
