            "text": "### 📐 Structural Wireframe Model Built\n\nI have constructed the two-storey U-shaped structural wireframe for the Courtyard Learning Centre in the Architectural workspace, verified all geometry and openings, saved the project record, mounted it in Model mode as a wireframe scene, and captured the live 3D view.\n\n---\n\n### 🏛️ Hierarchy and Layout\n\n```mindmap\nAB-01 Courtyard Learning Centre\n  Ground Floor (0.0 m to 3.6 m)\n    8 exterior boundary walls\n    250 mm ground floor slab\n    Open southern courtyard (12 m x 12 m)\n  Upper Floor (3.6 m to 7.2 m)\n    8 exterior boundary walls\n    250 mm floor slab panels\n    Stairwell opening (1.2 m x 7.2 m)\n  Roof (7.2 m)\n    3 flat roof zones (0 pitch, 0 eaves)\n    Courtyard unroofed\n```\n\n---\n\n### 🧱 Level and Element Verification\n\n#### 1. Storey Levels\n* **Ground Floor** (`a7a0093e-ae22-4bd8-88f0-ba49a3bde758`): Elevation `0 mm`, height `3600 mm`.\n* **Upper Floor** (`df8252dd-c9ca-4a2a-a764-52a2034902d6`): Elevation `3600 mm`, height `3600 mm`.\n\n#### 2. Exterior Boundary Walls (8 per level, 16 total)\nEach wall is 3600 mm high, tracking the 24 m × 18 m outer U-shape with a 12 m × 12 m open south courtyard:\n* **West wing south wall**: (0, 0) to (6000, 0) mm — Ground `2a1433fb-fe5b-47f2-9720-9b7836be5ffd`, Upper `f7b3058f-82b6-4b13-80f2-b32ec0545f7d` (6.0 m).\n* **Courtyard west inner wall**: (6000, 0) to (6000, 12000) mm — Ground `34326fca-431a-4d4f-be51-dd34f0920a26`, Upper `a426e762-5999-472e-a230-f8b7900bd4b1` (12.0 m).\n* **Courtyard north inner wall**: (6000, 12000) to (18000, 12000) mm — Ground `201b0d64-fd2d-48c2-b675-f46879c6481c`, Upper `a920f31e-947c-478c-a2bf-d4880b929f3c` (12.0 m).\n* **Courtyard east inner wall**: (18000, 12000) to (18000, 0) mm — Ground `692a190a-c78c-4574-87cb-93fec89f700d`, Upper `33108938-bb25-4575-948f-a39b0fc937ed` (12.0 m).\n* **East wing south wall**: (18000, 0) to (24000, 0) mm — Ground `6f246fc6-fba2-4b5c-8091-bbe2e07347ff`, Upper `c4943dec-9e43-44f4-9b5b-ab012a269f88` (6.0 m).\n* **East wing outer wall**: (24000, 0) to (24000, 18000) mm — Ground `89b5ba53-2853-4b27-8946-07f894a94d87`, Upper `c08cee0c-7f70-4d63-9b78-c59d8b23a3dc` (18.0 m).\n* **North wing outer wall**: (24000, 18000) to (0, 18000) mm — Ground `95bfd96f-24bf-47c7-9b30-33aa1543507e`, Upper `eb5a2608-e831-49df-b931-8af384d75e44` (24.0 m).\n* **West wing outer wall**: (0, 18000) to (0, 0) mm — Ground `0c36c356-ef2d-4fc6-bfb9-d97b476bff2e`, Upper `b0ecba24-8c98-406f-811c-127ac4ff33f9` (18.0 m).\n\n#### 3. Slabs and Stairwell Void\n* **Ground floor slab** (`afb1a1c4-2d7f-429d-b34d-d0101a98dbfa`): Continuous 250 mm thick concrete slab following the 8-point U-footprint, top at elevation 0 mm.\n* **Stairwell opening**: Positioned at X: [2400, 3600] mm and Y: [5400, 12600] mm inside the west wing. This reserves exactly 1.2 m × 7.2 m, providing 2.4 m clear passage on both sides and 5.4 m clear floor space at both north and south ends.\n* **Upper floor slab panels**: Because native slabs cannot hold negative internal voids within a single perimeter, the upper floor (top at 3.6 m, thickness 250 mm) is framed around the stairwell void using six contiguous rectangular slabs:\n  * South west wing (`2aea528a-1407-4943-a7db-fc79dbda3a02`): [0, 6000] × [0, 5400] mm.\n  * West flank strip (`b951177d-2107-43b0-ba15-9980bb2346e9`): [0, 2400] × [5400, 12600] mm.\n  * East flank strip (`dae85a4a-cb35-45cf-9e39-2bb84ab722e1`): [3600, 6000] × [5400, 12600] mm.\n  * North west wing (`91409341-a494-4ae8-8352-79ab0a7fddfa`): [0, 6000] × [12600, 18000] mm.\n  * North wing (`d539f8fa-d54e-41ea-9a40-6a84d9df9fe6`): [6000, 18000] × [12000, 18000] mm.\n  * East wing (`48ca270a-cb74-4614-81f9-603434b4ac05`): [18000, 24000] × [0, 18000] mm.\n\n#### 4. Flat Roof\n* System constraints require roof boundaries to be convex zones. The concave U-footprint flat roof (elevation 7.2 m, 0 mm eaves, 0° pitch) was placed using three contiguous rectangular zones on the Upper Floor level with a 3600 mm vertical offset:\n  * West wing roof (`f67ad274-6369-4a33-88a7-d4eb106fd9b5`): [0, 6000] × [0, 18000] mm.\n  * North wing roof (`2e85a2a3-a6d3-4ac9-82c1-6887c72eafc9`): [6000, 18000] × [12000, 18000] mm.\n  * East wing roof (`1fd2d1c1-ae75-436c-8d89-b1d5d57f6fab`): [18000, 24000] × [0, 18000] mm.\n* The 12 m × 12 m courtyard remains completely open to the sky.\n\n---\n\n### 📋 Technical Disclosures and Blockers\n\n* **Unsupported void cutouts**: Architectural slabs do not accept isolated interior void rings. The stairwell penetration was modelled by subdividing the upper floor slab into modular panels around the 1.2 m × 7.2 m void.\n* **Convex roof constraint**: Roof geometry requires convex polygons; a monolithic concave U-shape was resolved into three abutting convex roof rectangles.\n* **Wall assembly**: All 16 boundary walls utilize the unpriced default 260 mm multi-layer assembly (110 mm brick, 50 mm cavity, 90 mm stud, 10 mm plasterboard).\n* **Data status**: As specified in the work packet, this is an illustrative, unverified internal draft design without governing source calibration or professional engineering sign-off."
